   "text": {
    "L1": "In the evenings, the children play ball next to a creek in their neighbour's field.",
    "L2": "The title does not name a child or the team that scores most. Night is the winner.",
    "L3": "As the sky turns dark, the game is over because darkness ends the playing.",
    "L4": "The one-word lines make us read in gasps, like a child out of breath.",
    "L5": "When the poem says the trees creep close, the trees do not really move.",
    "L6": "They only seem nearer in the dark, so this is personification.",
    "L7": "The poem is free verse. It has no regular rhyme scheme.",
    "L8": "Now choose who wins and explain why."
   },
